<title>USA: TABLE-Allied Holdings Q2 shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Allied Holdings Q2 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>DECATUR, Ga. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Thousands, Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>    For the 3 mos. ended June 30		 1997	  1996</p>
<p> Revenues					   $112,576   $107,169</p>
<p> Net income					    3,513	3,098</p>
<p> Earnings per share				   0.45	 0.40</p>
<p> Wtd. avg. common shares outstanding	   7,725	7,725</p>
<p>    For the 6 mos. ended June 30		 1997	  1996</p>
<p> Revenues					   $208,969   $200,565</p>
<p> Income before extraordinary item		3,711	3,458</p>
<p> Net income					    3,711	2,523</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>  Income before extraordinary item		0.48	 0.45</p>
<p>  Net income					    0.48	 0.33</p>
<p> Wtd. avg. common shares outstanding	   7,725	7,725</p>
<p>Full company name is Allied Holdings Inc.</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said increase in revenues and earnings in 1997 was primarily due to an increase of about 5.0 percent in number of vehicles delivered.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
